---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /brand.html
title: "Brand mark — ZT monogram"
description: "The ZT monogram for Zachery Taylor's site (N1, Ligature), with its favicon and app icons, plus the options explored along the way."
sheet: B-001
sheetTitle: "Brand — the ZT mark"
noSitemap: true
noindex: true
rounds:
  - title: "Fresh concepts — N1–N8"
    label: "B-006"
    silhouette: true
    options:
      - key: n1
        name: "N1 · Ligature"
        note: "A pure ZT ligature with no container: one sharp top stroke is both the Z's top and the T's crossbar, medium-bold, optically centred."
      - key: n2
        name: "N2 · Monoline"
        note: "Frame and letters share one precise line weight, like an architect's stamp: square-cut ends, sharp corners, generous margin inside the frame."
      - key: n3
        name: "N3 · Negative space"
        note: "ZT knocked out of a solid blue square with subtly chamfered corners: two equal, sharp letters with a clean channel between them."
      - key: n4
        name: "N4 · Step"
        note: "The Z's bottom stroke runs on to become the T's crossbar, so the mark steps down from top-left to bottom-right: one shared line, the flow of the lot split."
      - key: n5
        name: "N5 · Engineered serif"
        note: "A serif/engineered hybrid: hairline-thin bars, heavy stems and diagonal, and small 45° wedge serifs, precise as lettering on a drawing."
      - key: n6
        name: "N6 · Dimension"
        note: "Sharp ZT standing on one architectural dimension line with 45° ticks: the drafting reference is a single quiet rule that drops away at small sizes."
      - key: n7
        name: "N7 · Section cut"
        note: "The ligature knocked out of a sharp blue square and sliced by one hairline section line, the cut every plan set is read through."
      - key: n8
        name: "N8 · Column"
        note: "An abstract structural symbol: the silhouette is a bold T, a beam on its column, and the Z is carved through the column as negative space."
  - title: "Smooth lot split — L1–L6"
    label: "B-005"
    silhouette: true
    options:
      - key: l1
        name: "L1 · Shared stroke"
        note: "One smooth top stroke is both the Z's top and the T's crossbar; equal-width letters, optically centred, splitting the rounded parcel into two near-equal lots."
      - key: l2
        name: "L2 · Touching"
        note: "Two identical-width smooth letters whose round ends meet on the lot line, optically centred so neither side of the parcel feels heavier."
      - key: l3
        name: "L3 · Centre line (symmetric)"
        note: "The strictly symmetric version: equal margins on all four sides, equal-width letters, and the gap exactly on the vertical axis, so the two lots are exactly equal."
      - key: l4
        name: "L4 · Sharp parcel, heavy"
        note: "The heaviest stroke on a square-cornered survey parcel: two equal letters with a small gap for the lot line, optically centred."
      - key: l5
        name: "L5 · Outlined parcel"
        note: "Plat-map version: a heavy rounded boundary line on paper, with the smooth blue ZT (equal letters, small gap) optically centred inside it."
      - key: l6
        name: "L6 · Soft curves"
        note: "The Z's diagonal eases through a gentle S-curve, like a road winding between the two lots; equal letters with a gap, optically centred."
  - title: "Lot split — variants of I"
    label: "B-004"
    silhouette: true
    options:
      - key: i1
        name: "I1 · Frontage + lot line"
        note: "Refined I: the Z road runs edge to edge (exactly two lots), its lower run is the frontage and the T's crossbar, and a lot line forms the stem."
      - key: i2
        name: "I2 · Shared lot line"
        note: "The road enters along the top (one stroke for the Z top and T crossbar) and leaves through the T's stem, the line the two lots share."
      - key: i3
        name: "I3 · Bronze road"
        note: "I1's two-lot frontage split with the right-of-way picked out in bronze on the blue parcel."
      - key: i4
        name: "I4 · Cul-de-sac"
        note: "The T's stem becomes a dead-end street ending in a cul-de-sac bulb inside the lower lot."
      - key: i5
        name: "I5 · Ink, sharp corners"
        note: "I2's shared-lot-line split on an ink parcel with sharp survey corners: the most graphic, stamp-like version."
      - key: i6
        name: "I6 · Plat map"
        note: "Outlined parcel on paper: heavy ink boundary, blue road, plus a thin dashed property line and bearing tick that drop out at small sizes."
      - key: i7
        name: "I7 · Circle parcel"
        note: "I1's frontage split inside a round parcel, like a site-location bubble or a hard-hat decal."
      - key: i8
        name: "I8 · Shield parcel"
        note: "I2's shared-lot-line split inside the route-marker shield: badge-like, strongest on a hard hat or a truck door."
  - title: "Round 3 — statement marks"
    label: "B-003"
    silhouette: true
    options:
      - key: h
        name: "H · Contour line"
        note: "One continuous heavy line draws the Z, with no stacked layers. Its top stroke ends in a survey point, so stroke and point read as the crossbar of a T, with the diagonal as its stem. The most minimal of the set: two strokes of a pen."
      - key: i
        name: "I · Lot split"
        note: "A square parcel split by a Z-shaped right-of-way that enters on the left and exits on the right. The road's lower run is the frontage, and a lot line dropping from it forms the T. Solid shape, negative-space letters."
      - key: j
        name: "J · Section cut"
        note: "The section-cut marker from every plan set, a circle plus its view arrow, with a heavy ZT ligature standing on the cut line that splits the marker. The teardrop silhouette alone is recognisable at 16 px."
      - key: k
        name: "K · Route shield"
        note: "A highway route-marker shield with a heavy ZT ligature (one shared top stroke) cut out of it. Roads, signage, infrastructure. Reads like a badge on a hard hat and holds up as a one-colour stamp."
  - title: "Round 2 — new directions"
    label: "B-002"
    options:
      - key: d
        name: "D · North arrow"
        note: "A surveyor's north arrow in a compass ring. The T is the arrow — half-filled north point, crossbar, shaft — and its crossbar doubles as the top of a bronze Z. Most ‘survey plat’ of the set."
      - key: e
        name: "E · Contour lines"
        note: "ZT as a ridge on a topographic map: the letters are the high ground and contour lines step out around them, merging where the letters meet, with a bronze index contour outermost."
      - key: f
        name: "F · Lettering stencil"
        note: "Bold stencil ZT cut from an ink lettering template (think Leroy guide), with stencil bridges, a scale along the bottom edge, and a bronze registration hole. The most minimal and graphic."
      - key: g
        name: "G · Firm block"
        note: "A drawing sheet's firm block: heavy outer border, medium divider, fine rule. In the nav it becomes a horizontal lockup — ZT cell, then Zachery Taylor over Civil Designer · EI. The square ZT cell is the favicon."
  - title: "Round 1"
    label: "B-001"
    options:
      - key: a
        name: "A · Title block"
        note: "Z and T share one top stroke, set inside a blueprint sheet frame with a title-block strip — the drawing-set motif used across the site."
      - key: b
        name: "B · Serif ligature"
        note: "Instrument Serif Z overlapped by an italic blueprint-blue T, on paper with a bronze rule. The most literary — leans toward the book."
      - key: c
        name: "C · Benchmark"
        note: "A survey benchmark disk: graduated ring, section-marker circle split by a datum line, ZT above and a benchmark triangle below."
---
{%- import "macros.njk" as ui with context -%}
<style>
  .mono-grid { display: grid; gap: 28px; }
  .mono { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr 1fr; border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; background: rgb(var(--surface) / .8); }
  .mono > div { padding: 26px; }
  .mono .info h2 { font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .mono .info p { color: var(--muted); font-size: .95rem; }
  .mono .current { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 10px; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--action); color: #fff; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .swatch { display: grid; gap: 18px; align-content: start; }
  .swatch.light { background: #f3f0e8; color: #0f1419; --mark-ink: #0f1419; --mark-accent: #0a4f9c; }
  .swatch.dark { background: #0f1419; color: #f3f0e8; --mark-ink: #f3f0e8; --mark-accent: #8ab8f0; }
  .swatch .k { font-size: .66rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; opacity: .75; }
  .big svg { width: 168px; height: 168px; }
  .row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; }
  .tab { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 7px 12px; border-radius: 9px 9px 0 0; background: #fff; color: #333; font-size: .78rem; box-shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.08); }
  .dark .tab { background: #262c33; color: #ddd; }
  .tab svg { width: 16px; height: 16px; }
  .fav32 svg { width: 32px; height: 32px; }
  .navmock { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; font-weight: 700; font-size: .95rem; }
  .navmock svg { width: 40px; height: 40px; }
  .navmock.lockupmock svg { width: auto; height: 40px; }
  .big-lockup svg { width: 100%; max-width: 340px; height: auto; }
  .round-title { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 14px; margin: 8px 0 -6px; }
  .round-title h2 { font-size: 1.7rem; }
  .navmock small { display: block; font-size: .62rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; opacity: .7; }
  .sil { display: grid; gap: 8px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .sil .k { font-size: .66rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--grey-text); }
  .sil-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }
  .sil-box { display: inline-flex; align-items: flex-end; gap: 10px; padding: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; }
  .sil-box.inv { background: #0f1419; }
  .sil-box.inv img { filter: invert(1); }
  .mono-selected { border-color: var(--action); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .explored > summary { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; padding: 8px 18px; border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: 999px; background: rgb(var(--surface) / .8); font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; }
  .explored[open] > summary { margin-bottom: 28px; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .mono { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
<header class="page-header">
  <div class="wrap">
    {{ ui.sectionLabel("B-001", "Brand") }}
    <h1>The ZT <em>mark.</em></h1>
    <p class="lead">The selected mark is <strong>N1 · Ligature</strong>: one sharp top stroke is both the Z’s top and the T’s crossbar, medium-bold, with no container. It’s live in the navigation, the footer title block, the 404 page, the résumé, the social share card, and every favicon and app icon.</p>
  </div>
</header>
{%- set sel = site.monogram %}
<section class="band" aria-labelledby="sel-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    {{ ui.sectionLabel("B-010", "Selected mark") }}
    <h2 id="sel-title" class="visually-hidden">Selected mark</h2>
    <article class="mono mono-selected" aria-labelledby="opt-sel">
      <div class="info">
        <span class="current">SELECTED</span>
        <h2 id="opt-sel">{{ sel | upper }} · Ligature</h2>
        <p>Blue on paper, light blue on ink: container-less, so it takes its colours from the page (and from the device’s light/dark setting when it’s a browser-tab favicon). Raster favicons and app icons put it on a blue tile so it reads on any browser chrome or home screen.</p>
        <div class="sil" aria-label="Icons">
          <span class="k">Tile · app icon · one colour</span>
          <div class="sil-row">
            <span class="sil-box"><img src="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ sel }}-tile.svg" width="84" height="84" alt="N1 on a blue tile (favicon)"><img src="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ sel }}-tile.svg" width="16" height="16" alt=""></span>
            <span class="sil-box"><img src="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ sel }}-app.svg" width="84" height="84" alt="N1 app icon" style="border-radius:18px"></span>
            <span class="sil-box"><img src="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ sel }}-mono.svg" width="84" height="84" alt="N1 as a black silhouette"><img src="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ sel }}-mono.svg" width="16" height="16" alt=""></span>
            <span class="sil-box inv"><img src="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ sel }}-mono.svg" width="84" height="84" alt="N1 as a white silhouette"><img src="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ sel }}-mono.svg" width="16" height="16" alt=""></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top:14px"><a href="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ sel }}.svg">Mark SVG</a> · <a href="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ sel }}-mono.svg">One-colour SVG</a> · <a href="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ sel }}-tile.svg">Tile SVG</a> · <a href="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ sel }}-app.svg">App icon SVG</a> · <a href="/assets/brand/og-default.png">Share card</a></p>
      </div>
      {%- for tone in ["light", "dark"] %}
      <div class="swatch {{ tone }}">
        <span class="k">{{ "On paper" if tone == "light" else "On ink" }}</span>
        <div class="row"><span class="tab">{{ sel | monogram | safe }} Zachery Taylor</span><span class="fav32">{{ sel | monogram | safe }}</span></div>
        <span class="navmock">{{ sel | monogram | safe }}<span>Zachery Taylor<small>Civil Designer · EI</small></span></span>
        <div class="big">{{ sel | monogram | safe }}</div>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="band" aria-labelledby="explored-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    {{ ui.sectionLabel("B-020", "Explored options") }}
    <h2 id="explored-title">Explored <em>options.</em></h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Every direction considered on the way to N1, newest round first, kept for reference.</p>
    <details class="explored">
      <summary>Show all {% set n = 0 %}{% for r in rounds %}{% set n = n + r.options.length %}{% endfor %}{{ n }} explored options</summary>
  <div class="mono-grid">
    {%- for r in rounds %}
    <div class="round-title">{{ ui.sectionLabel(r.label, r.title) }}</div>
    {%- for o in r.options %}
    {%- set lk = o.key | lockup %}
    <article class="mono" aria-labelledby="opt-{{ o.key }}">
      <div class="info">
        {%- if o.key == site.monogram %}<span class="current">SELECTED</span>{% endif %}
        <h2 id="opt-{{ o.key }}">{{ o.name }}</h2>
        <p>{{ o.note }}</p>
        <p style="margin-top:14px"><a href="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ o.key }}.svg">Download SVG</a>{% if lk %} · <a href="/assets/brand/lockup-{{ o.key }}.svg">Lockup SVG</a>{% endif %}{% if r.silhouette %} · <a href="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ o.key }}-mono.svg">One-colour SVG</a>{% endif %}</p>
        {%- if r.silhouette %}
        <div class="sil" aria-label="Single-colour silhouette">
          <span class="k">One colour</span>
          <div class="sil-row">
            <span class="sil-box"><img src="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ o.key }}-mono.svg" width="84" height="84" alt="Option {{ o.key | upper }} as a black silhouette"><img src="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ o.key }}-mono.svg" width="16" height="16" alt=""></span>
            <span class="sil-box inv"><img src="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ o.key }}-mono.svg" width="84" height="84" alt="Option {{ o.key | upper }} as a white silhouette"><img src="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ o.key }}-mono.svg" width="16" height="16" alt=""></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      {%- for tone in ["light", "dark"] %}
      <div class="swatch {{ tone }}">
        <span class="k">{{ "On paper" if tone == "light" else "On ink" }}</span>
        <div class="row"><span class="tab">{{ o.key | monogram | safe }} Zachery Taylor</span><span class="fav32">{{ o.key | monogram | safe }}</span></div>
        {%- if lk %}
        <span class="navmock lockupmock">{{ lk | safe }}</span>
        {%- else %}
        <span class="navmock">{{ o.key | monogram | safe }}<span>Zachery Taylor<small>Civil Designer · EI</small></span></span>
        {%- endif %}
        <div class="big">{{ o.key | monogram | safe }}</div>
        {%- if lk %}<div class="big-lockup">{{ lk | safe }}</div>{% endif %}
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </article>
    {%- endfor %}
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
